        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "93ae2fd3-b014-58ce-b3c1-5bc8f2625667",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Detroit\n- People: Kathryn Bigelow, Mark Boal, Will Poulter, Laz Alonso\n- Events: Algiers Motel incident, 1967 Detroit riot, Long Hot Summer of 1967\n- Places: Detroit, United States\n- Topics: period crime drama films, race riots\n\nFacts:\n- The 1967 Detroit riot, also called the 12th Street riot and the 1967 Detroit rebellion, was one of 159 race riots that swept cities across the United States during the Long Hot Summer of 1967.\n- Detroit is a 2017 American period crime drama film directed by Kathryn Bigelow and written by Mark Boal.\n- Detroit is based on the Algiers Motel incident during Detroit's 1967 12th Street Riot, and its release commemorated the event's 50th anniversary.\n- Will Poulter, born on 28 January 1993, is an English actor known for film roles including The Maze Runner, Son of Rambow, We're the Millers, The Revenant, and Detroit.\n- Laz Alonso has had film roles in Jarhead, This Christmas, Miracle at St. Anna, and Detroit.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
